Ancient Egypt explored via seven games, challenging memory and observation skills:
_ discover Nile and its flooding;
_ enter a pyramid and unveil wonderful treasures;
_ fill in the canopic jars;
_ be a master in mummification;
_ take part into the weighting of the heart ceremony;
_ learn how to decipher hieroglyphs;
_ learn about pharaohs and their society.
The blue scarab tab activates the narration, explaining important facts about pyramids, pharaohs and this fascinating ancient civilization. 

"Art Stories in Ancient Egypt" is safe and fun: its games and interactions take kids in a journey in space and time. A final quiz section tests what kids have learnt through play. 

This is a most useful app for learning through play, for enlivening your history homework, for learning more about this fascinating population!

WITH CHILDREN
Art Stories apps are designed to entertain children in an intelligent way, encouraging them to ask questions and to think. Children and adults can play with them together. For more information and for regularly updated ideas on how to use our apps, visit our website.

WHO ARE WE
Art Stories is a digital publisher that develops games about artistic and cultural heritage for children between 5 and 10 years old. With extensive experience of museum education, we are convinced that intelligent digital games spark users’ curiosity and consolidate their skills. Discovering food, cities, history and art is a great adventure for creative children all around the world. Our apps encourage children to look up from their tablets and discover the world.
